      (17,33,"`floor_guess`. Counts points per 5 cm height bin. The lidar on the Go2 is mounted upside down and sees the floor more than anything else, so the fullest bin is the floor. A dictionary is used instead of an array: one stray point 100 m away would otherwise force a huge array. The loop keeps the bin with the most points (on a tie, the lower one) and returns the middle of that bin."),
